---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="FIFGO and FIFGROUP, Glen Hutajulu"
  description="A customer app and public website revamp for one of Indonesia's consumer finance groups."
  caseStudy
>
  <div class="wrap">

    <header class="case-head">
      <h1 class="h-large">fifgo and fifgroup</h1>
      <p class="lede lede-wide mt-28">A customer app and public website revamp for one of Indonesia's consumer finance groups.</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="cover">
      <img class="img" src="/work/fifgo/cover.webp" alt="FIFGO app on a phone beside the FIFGROUP website on a laptop" width="2400" height="1600" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
    </figure>

    <section class="mt-24" aria-label="Project summary">
      <dl class="grid grid-260 summary">
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Problem</dt><dd class="small mt-10">The website and customer app could not generate quality leads. Product information was inadequate, and the application and monitoring journey was too long and complex.</dd></div>
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Role and team</dt><dd class="small mt-10">UI/UX Designer at Aleph, working in a project team.</dd></div>
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Outcome</dt><dd class="small mt-10">In UAT, users completed the loan flow in under 7 minutes with zero drop-off.</dd></div>
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Timeline</dt><dd class="small mt-10">Sep 2023 – Feb 2024. The app and website are both live.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>In mid-2023 FIFGROUP decided to revamp its website and consumer app, to keep up with technology, hold on to existing customers and win younger ones.</p>
      <p class="mt-14">Our answer was a set of tools that understand what people need, guide them through it and give them the confidence to go ahead.</p>

      <h2 class="h-section mt-72">starting with the people</h2>
      <p>We worked human-centred, in cycles of analyze, create and test, and started by listening to the business and its customers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-190 mt-40">
      <div class="card-grey grain"><p class="stat">38</p><p class="label mt-10">Stakeholder interviews</p></div>
      <div class="card-grey grain"><p class="stat">3</p><p class="label mt-10">Days of workshop</p></div>
      <div class="card-grey grain"><p class="stat">7</p><p class="label mt-10">Journeys audited</p></div>
      <div class="card-grey grain"><p class="stat">4</p><p class="label mt-10">Personas created</p></div>
      <div class="card-grey grain"><p class="stat">12</p><p class="label mt-10">User test participants</p></div>
      <div class="card-grey grain"><p class="stat">2</p><p class="label mt-10">Cities for user testing</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">four people, one worry</h2>
      <p>Taking on a loan is a big decision. Each persona was stuck in a different place, but all of them needed clearer information before they could commit. Across the research, security, relevancy and accountability mattered most.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-280 mt-40">
      <div class="card card-line grain">
        <h3 class="h-card">young striver</h3>
        <p class="label mt-6">Yoga, 24</p>
        <p class="small mt-16">Struggles to decide among too many unreliable loan options and fears unnecessary expenses.</p>
        <p class="small soft mt-12">Needs step-by-step guidance and a clear amount and duration to pay.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-line grain">
        <h3 class="h-card">family treasurer</h3>
        <p class="label mt-6">Fatima, 37</p>
        <p class="small mt-16">Overwhelmed by detail and a long approval process, and can't find the product that fits.</p>
        <p class="small soft mt-12">Needs digestible information and the ability to pick up where she left off.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-line grain">
        <h3 class="h-card">assistance seeker</h3>
        <p class="label mt-6">Ahmad, 44</p>
        <p class="small mt-16">Finds apps and manual form filling a hassle, and feels lost completing a journey online.</p>
        <p class="small soft mt-12">Needs to be recognised as an existing customer and given relevant recommendations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-line grain">
        <h3 class="h-card">opportunity chaser</h3>
        <p class="label mt-6">Okta, 34</p>
        <p class="small mt-16">Very busy, wants to anticipate the risk of failure, and needs assurance before committing.</p>
        <p class="small soft mt-12">Needs flexible appointments and a tangible amount and loan duration.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">three moments that mattered</h2>
      <p>We mapped the main customer journey into three phases and set what each one had to become.</p>

      <div class="phases mt-28">
        <div class="phase">
          <p class="label">Discovery</p>
          <h3 class="phase-title mt-8">Be the effective discovery channel.</h3>
          <p class="small soft mt-8">Promo offers felt aggressive and disturbing. Customers wanted relevant, trusted offers at the right moment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="phase">
          <p class="label">Application</p>
          <h3 class="phase-title mt-8">Boost efficiency so sales can focus on converting bookings.</h3>
          <p class="small soft mt-8">Online applications were dominated by unintentional leads. Potential customers needed a simple, reliable process that encouraged them to apply.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="phase">
          <p class="label">Monitoring</p>
          <h3 class="phase-title mt-8">Build a good relationship with good-performing customers.</h3>
          <p class="small soft mt-8">Reach to good-performing customers was low. They needed a trusted channel that gave them assurance about their finances.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="quote mt-40">How might we provide a proactive, practical and clear platform for our users?</p>

      <h2 class="h-section mt-72">shorter steps to a loan</h2>
      <p>To reduce the struggle in applying, the journey now runs straight from simulation into application, personal data is prefilled through OCR, and the form focuses on essential information.</p>
      <p class="mt-14">The loan simulation works from either direction. People can start from the motorcycle they want, or from what they can afford each month, so they see a realistic amount and duration before committing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band mt-band" aria-label="Loan simulation">
    <figure class="fig-900">
      <img class="img" src="/work/fifgo/loan-simulation.webp" alt="Loan simulation screens, by dream motorcycle and by monthly ability to pay" width="1540" height="1214" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption class="label mt-10">Simulate by dream motorcycle or by ability to pay</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">a contract you can actually read</h2>
      <p>I revamped the mobile app's full loan-contract experience: application, payment, contract renewal, late fees and contract management. The old contract page was one long list of equally weighted labels and numbers, so we restructured the information around what customers look for first.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="fig-900 mt-md">
      <img class="img" src="/work/fifgo/contract-before-after.webp" alt="Contract detail page before and after the redesign" width="1600" height="1500" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
    </figure>

    <div class="ann mt-lg">
      <div class="ann-wrap">
        <div class="rel">
          <img class="ann-img" src="/work/fifgo/contract-full.webp" alt="Full redesigned contract detail page" width="517" height="2316" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
          <span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 1.55%; top: 0.35%; width: 95.36%; height: 9.93%"></span>
          <span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 5.03%; top: 11.74%; width: 90.14%; height: 8.29%"></span>
          <span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 5.03%; top: 20.38%; width: 90.14%; height: 8.98%"></span>
          <span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 1.55%; top: 30.22%; width: 96.91%; height: 43.35%"></span>
          <span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 1.55%; top: 74.53%; width: 96.91%; height: 19.69%"></span>
          <span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 6.19%; top: 95.16%; width: 87.81%; height: 3.54%"></span>
          <span class="ann-line" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 96.91%; top: 5.31%"><span class="ann-dot"></span></span>
          <span class="ann-line" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 95.16%; top: 15.89%"><span class="ann-dot"></span></span>
          <span class="ann-line" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 95.16%; top: 24.87%"><span class="ann-dot"></span></span>
          <span class="ann-line" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 98.45%; top: 51.90%"><span class="ann-dot"></span></span>
          <span class="ann-line" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 98.45%; top: 84.37%"><span class="ann-dot"></span></span>
          <span class="ann-line" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 94.00%; top: 96.93%"><span class="ann-dot"></span></span>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div class="ann-item" style="top: 5.31%"><dt class="ann-title">sticky header</dt><dd class="soft mt-6">A simplified, easy-to-find contract name and number.</dd></div>
          <div class="ann-item" style="top: 15.89%"><dt class="ann-title">highlighted remaining bill</dt><dd class="soft mt-6">The most important information about the bill comes first.</dd></div>
          <div class="ann-item" style="top: 24.87%"><dt class="ann-title">cross-selling card</dt><dd class="soft mt-6">Customers about to finish a contract see other loan products at the right moment.</dd></div>
          <div class="ann-item" style="top: 51.90%"><dt class="ann-title">clear contract structure</dt><dd class="soft mt-6">Contract information reads easily with better categorised sections.</dd></div>
          <div class="ann-item" style="top: 84.37%"><dt class="ann-title">quick actions</dt><dd class="soft mt-6">A dedicated section with visual icons, so the available actions are clear.</dd></div>
          <div class="ann-item" style="top: 96.93%"><dt class="ann-title">floating payment button</dt><dd class="soft mt-6">Nobody has to scroll to the bottom of the page to pay.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band mt-lg" aria-label="App screens">
    <div class="inner grid grid-240">
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-9-19" src="/work/fifgo/app-home.webp" alt="FIFGO home screen with a motorcycle loan contract card" width="780" height="1688" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Home, contracts first</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-9-19" src="/work/fifgo/app-contract.webp" alt="FIFGO contract detail screen with contract, cost and vehicle sections" width="628" height="2576" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Contract detail</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-9-19" src="/work/fifgo/app-explore.webp" alt="FIFGO explore screen with product shortcuts, recommendations and daily check-in" width="780" height="5477" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Explore, products and rewards</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">a website with more to say</h2>
      <p>On the corporate side, stakeholders wanted FIFGROUP's online presence and content to feel more engaging. Inadequate product information was also part of the original problem, so the product page now leads with what someone wants to buy, then explains why to choose FIFASTRA, the four application steps and what to prepare. The group homepage starts from what the visitor needs and routes them to the right financing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-320 mt-md">
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-4-5" src="/work/fifgo/web-fifastra.webp" alt="FIFASTRA product page with motorcycle search, benefits, application steps and offers" width="1600" height="4120" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">FIFASTRA product page</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-4-5" src="/work/fifgo/web-fifgroup.webp" alt="FIFGROUP homepage with financing categories and need-based recommendations" width="1600" height="4902" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">FIFGROUP homepage</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">one visual language</h2>
      <p>An icon set carries both function and character, and the same components keep the design consistent across every digital platform.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="split mt-md">
      <figure class="panel panel-icons grain">
        <img class="img" src="/work/fifgo/icons.webp" alt="Custom icon set for FIFGROUP" width="980" height="840" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
      </figure>
      <figure class="panel panel-parts grain">
        <img class="img" src="/work/fifgo/components.webp" alt="Reusable app components such as contract cards and payment summaries" width="1600" height="889" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">result</h2>
      <p>In UAT, users completed the loan flow in under 7 minutes with zero drop-off. The FIFGO app and the FIFGROUP website have both been released.</p>
      <p class="mt-40"><a href="/#work">Back to all work</a></p>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>
